Z||000000||Cheever2||07-04-2001||12:15 PM|||| <A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank>http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay</A> <P>At least the name reflects what it's about.<BR>The navigation buttons at the top are apparently inserted automatically by the software I'm using - MS Picture-It! 2001 Platinum - do NOT buy that for webpage building!  It relies entirely on onscreen instructions, and is terrible for trying to get answers.  Anyway, I filed an incident report with Microsoft regarding those buttons but I won't expect a satisfactory reply.  I will try building this on Broderbund's website designer soon.<P>Also, I am having difficulty connecting to the Fiero email list so that I can sign up just long enough to send the form letter I wrote to inform them of the Parts Relay.  Is there a forum member already on the list who would volunteer to do that for me?  I'll email the form letter to you.  It's a simple cut & paste.<P>I'm forgetting something, but I'll post again when I think of it.  <P><P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cheever2||07-22-2001||06:46 PM||||I finally got on the Fiero List and sent out an invitation to join the Parts Relay.  I immediately got 4 new members, in: Iowa, Indiana, Michigan and Eastern PA.<P>Now, has anybody been keeping a list of all the Fiero clubs?  I made such a list last year, but was not able to keep it updated.  I want to send the invitation to each of them.  Who's got the best list?<P><BR>  <P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator||||reg||1
